WEBVTT

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:00.740
How horrible.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.870
It's an emergency!

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:05.750
Get the dogs out!

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:11.880
<i>Ryuukou Yanagi.</i>

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:19.300
<i>One of the strongest,</i>
<i>most evil death row inmates.</i>

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:25.060
<i>He broke out of prison like this before</i>
<i>and came to Tokyo.</i>

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.850
<i>Emergency!</i>

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:31.980
<i>He has a small build</i>
<i>that doesn't even reach 160cm.</i>

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:36.820
<i>But by instantly creating a vacuum</i>
<i>in the palm of his hand,</i>

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:38.740
<i>he can break strengthened glass</i>

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:42.820
<i>and make strong men faint in a heartbeat.</i>

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:47.080
<i>And with his lethal poison hands,</i>

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:50.460
<i>he is even able to</i>
<i>send his opponents to death.</i>

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:55.550
<i>After getting through many fights,</i>

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.800
<i>he lost both his arms to Izou Motobe</i>

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:05.100
<i>and was destroyed</i>
<i>with one attack from Yujiro Hanma.</i>

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:15.320
<i>This is the only surviving prison officer</i>
<i>who was at Yanagi's prison break.</i>

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:19.280
<i>He should be able to tell me</i>
<i>what happened.</i>

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:22.110
It's impossible.

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:25.200
<i>Even God...</i>

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.450
<i>would be fooled by him.</i>

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.710
<i>He has been like that</i>
<i>ever since he came in.</i>

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.790
<i>His skin was half acrylic.</i>

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:37.750
<i>He'd stare vacantly at one spot.</i>

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.260
<i>Or maybe he wasn't looking at anything.</i>

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:43.970
<i>He wouldn't say a word.</i>

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.640
<i>Even a plant would be livelier.</i>

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:54.350
<i>His transfer to a normal hospital</i>
<i>was a unanimous decision.</i>

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:02.200
Hey old man, can you move?

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.200
<i>I'll never forget what I saw...</i>

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.620
<i>from outside that cell.</i>

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:15.880
Of course I can move.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.380
<i>The sheets danced violently.</i>

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.340
<i>There were blood spurts and screams.</i>

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:27.680
<i>When the sheets fluttered down,</i>

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:30.680
<i>Ryuukou Yanagi was gone.</i>

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:39.110
SEVERAL DAYS LATER

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:41.230
<i>Inspector Sonoda, coming through.</i>

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:43.780
SUPERINTENDENT GENERAL'S OFFICE

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:45.740
I saw your report.

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:49.120
-What happened to him?
-Sir.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:53.040
After his escape,
his whereabouts are completely unknown.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:58.750
I thought the death row inmates' case
was all over.

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:01.550
At least, that's what I heard.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:02.920
You are correct.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:06.050
That's what we thought as well.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:09.550
How are the other death row inmates?

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:12.310
What do you mean?

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:15.230
If Yanagi escaped his cell,

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:20.360
shouldn't you check on
the other inmates' whereabouts as well?

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:21.980
It's as you say.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:23.570
Hurry it up.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:25.490
Yes, sir.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:36.460
I'm surprised Dorian is being held here.

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:42.250
Dorian is a death row inmate
who has killed many.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:47.470
But he was once a Sea King who
mastered kung fu here at Bailin Temple.

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:52.640
We took him in because of
our old ties with him.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:54.930
<i>Dorian.</i>

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:02.520
<i>He is also one of the strongest, most evil</i>
<i>death row inmates who came to Tokyo.</i>

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:09.820
<i>He fights by using the many weapons</i>
<i>and tools he hides in his body.</i>

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:16.950
<i>He also uses hypnotism</i>

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:20.170
<i>which lets him control his opponents.</i>

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:28.930
<i>But Dorian took one hit</i>
<i>from Sea King Retsu</i>

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:30.180
<i>and finally met defeat.</i>

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.260
<i>I already knew.</i>

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:36.100
<i>This life of mine,</i>
<i>supposedly colored by victory</i>

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:40.900
<i>was in fact a path to darkness.</i>

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:42.810
<i>And since then,</i>

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:48.240
<i>he should've regressed back to</i>
<i>the mind of a toddler.</i>

00:06:58.040 --> 00:06:59.040
Look.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:06.340
He's in here.

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:19.640
Dorian is painting a picture?

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:23.150
And this painting is candy?

00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:26.270
Yes, it's a painting of candy.

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:29.610
I wonder how many of these he has drawn.

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:31.650
He only draws candy.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:33.530
He's good at it.

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:37.870
They sell well and at quite the price.

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:40.540
Those paintings sell well?

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:42.920
That's right. However,

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:48.130
the problem is that form of his.

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:50.670
Is it some kind of training?

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.010
Yes.

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:56.430
It's a Chinese martial arts exercise
that strengthens your lower body.

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:59.180
It's called the <i>zhan zhuang.</i>

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:01.810
And his squat is so deep.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:04.940
How long has he been doing this?

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:08.440
It's based on that.

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:17.200
A mountain of candy?

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:22.710
He won't stop until he eats all of it.

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:25.960
As a result,
his lower body looks like that.

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:30.590
He has gained 20kg
since he started his rehabilitation.

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:35.220
I wonder if this can
even be called rehabilitation.

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:41.720
<i>Dorian's actions...</i>

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:45.480
<i>aren't for rehabilitation at all.</i>

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:47.980
<i>He's preparing.</i>

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:51.480
<i>He's preparing for something big.</i>

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:56.780
<i>It looked to me</i>
<i>as if he were meticulously preparing.</i>

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:05.620
I was told of your arrival.
Right this way.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:11.750
It's been like this since
the budget cuts from back then.

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:14.840
Even the lights are in horrible condition.

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:21.430
Although, I guess lights and sound
don't matter to Doyle.

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:23.350
-Sound?
-Yes.

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:27.140
He ruptured his eardrums on his own.

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:33.900
<i>He ruptured his eardrums?</i>

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:37.110
Doyle is blind, if I recall correctly.

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:41.370
<i>Doyle.</i>

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:45.330
<i>He is also one of the strongest,</i>
<i>most evil death row inmates.</i>

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:47.250
Mr. Unchained.

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:51.250
<i>By using weapons and ammo</i>
<i>buried in his body,</i>

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:53.550
<i>he turned himself into a weapon.</i>

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:55.800
Come at me. Come.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:31.670
<i>During his fight with the Shin Shin Kai,</i>
<i>his mental state changed</i>

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:35.590
<i>and Doyle finally knew</i>
<i>the taste of defeat.</i>

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:43.850
<i>But during the following fight,</i>
<i>he lost sight in both eyes</i>

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:47.520
<i>and was imprisoned in this medical prison.</i>

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:57.320
Why did Doyle, who is blind,
rupture his own eardrums?

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:59.450
I have absolutely no idea.

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:02.570
-Except...
-Except?

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:07.200
Doyle said something strange
when he entered this facility.

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:14.460
Well, he does have a disability,

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:16.500
-but he'll work--
-No!

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:20.220
-What?
-I have no disability whatsoever.

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:21.220
What?

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:23.970
I am complete.

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:29.480
By losing a monumental thing
we call "light,"

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:35.480
I've obtained a monumental treasure
that replaces that light.

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:36.980
Is that so?

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:38.980
And so, Chief...

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:41.610
Sound.

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:45.370
Sound is another important sense.

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:47.870
What if I exchange my sense of hearing?

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:50.370
Chief.

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:54.580
I wonder what I will obtain.

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:59.210
So with that,
Doyle ruptured his own eardrums.

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:03.970
Then what did he obtain exactly?

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:06.510
I'm not sure.

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:11.640
But it's been 1.5 years since he lost
hearing in both ears.

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:15.770
Based on recent reports
from the prison guards,

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:19.280
<i>Doyle did something strange in his cell.</i>

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:22.610
<i>He caught a bat.</i>

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:24.360
<i>A bat?</i>

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:29.870
<i>Yes. As you know,</i>
<i>the inside of these cells is filthy.</i>

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:31.540
<i>They're full of bugs.</i>

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:35.540
<i>The bats target them</i>
<i>and get lost in there.</i>

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:42.550
<i>He caught bats in the dark?</i>

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:47.550
<i>Yes, and it appears he said</i>
<i>something strange again.</i>

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:53.560
Oh, there's skin.

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:57.310
Jeez, I wonder what he meant.

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:01.400
<i>Doyle went to the trouble</i>
<i>of throwing away his hearing</i>

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:04.490
<i>and gained a keen sense of touch.</i>

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:09.660
<i>But for what purpose?</i>

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:17.920
Sikorsky?

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:20.880
He's an obedient one.

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:24.590
No, nothing dangerous has happened.

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:26.090
Is that so?

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:29.600
Although, if I had to say one thing...

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:30.850
What?

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:33.930
<i>Sikorsky.</i>

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:37.100
<i>He's also one of the strong,</i>
<i>evil death row inmates,</i>

00:13:37.190 --> 00:13:40.650
<i>easily escaping a prison</i>
<i>that was considered inescapable.</i>

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:46.610
<i>Using his body as a weapon,</i>
<i>he has hurt and killed many.</i>

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:48.530
Serves you right!

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:04.710
<i>Davai!</i>

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:35.660
<i>And Sikorsky should have</i>

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:39.830
<i>finally accepted his defeat.</i>

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:42.500
I lose!

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:46.510
Have mercy!

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:52.600
It's called pinching power, right?

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:54.510
Pinching power?

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:56.640
What kind of power is that?

00:14:57.600 --> 00:14:59.520
It's how strong your fingers can grip.

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:04.190
<i>And right when Ivan prayed for the imp,</i>

00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:10.700
<i>the imp plunged into the earth</i>
<i>like a stone into water.</i>

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:13.320
<i>Deep into the ground.</i>

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:21.750
Gripping, holding, and pinching
use power from your finger.

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:26.920
They say that you can bend a coin
with your fingers if you're amazing.

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:35.430
Oh, geez.

00:15:39.390 --> 00:15:40.940
Mr. Sikorsky.

00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:42.940
Can you return that?

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:45.560
We as staff don't get paid much.

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:48.280
Even a single coin is valuable to us.

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:53.950
Hey!

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:06.040
<i>It wasn't just bent.</i>

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:08.960
<i>It was balled up like scrap paper.</i>

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:12.220
Wow, I was astounded.

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:17.050
Okay, want to take a peek?

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:26.520
<i>He balled up a nickel coin</i>
<i>with his fingers.</i>

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:31.240
<i>You can do such things</i>
<i>if you have extreme pinching power.</i>

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:33.240
See?

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:36.910
He's gripping the wall.

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:39.990
It's a surface with nothing on it.

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:44.080
Not sure if he's sleeping or awake, but...

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:47.750
he stays like that until morning.

00:17:00.140 --> 00:17:01.560
It's Inspector Sonoda.

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:03.020
SUPERINTENDENT GENERAL'S OFFICE

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:04.100
Superintendent General?

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:08.560
The superintendent general is out.

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:10.400
Where to?

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:12.150
Actually...

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:21.410
<i>One of the death row inmates, Spec,</i>
<i>is imprisoned in this medical facility.</i>

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:26.290
I can hold my breath for five minutes.

00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:27.880
<i>Spec.</i>

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:31.380
<i>One of the strongest,</i>
<i>most evil death row inmates.</i>

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:36.720
<i>He has unimaginable physical ability.</i>

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:39.470
<i>After killing many people,</i>

00:17:39.550 --> 00:17:42.100
<i>he came to Japan.</i>

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:14.420
<i>But Spec lost in a lethal fight</i>
<i>against Kaoru Hanayama.</i>

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:18.260
<i>That defeat acted as a trigger,</i>

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:21.430
<i>and he experienced rapid aging.</i>

00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:25.140
<i>His true age was actually 97.</i>

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:29.770
<i>Spec is now bedridden.</i>

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:34.530
<i>That's why I put off investigating him.</i>

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:37.280
<i>Why is the general here?</i>

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:41.740
-Excuse me.
-Oh, Sonoda.

00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:44.620
They want you to see this too.

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:46.120
Please take a look.

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:50.040
This is Spec's thermography.

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:56.050
The muscles being used are shown by
colors that represent body temperature.

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:02.140
The heat from his shoulders

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:05.310
spread to both of his palms at once.

00:19:05.890 --> 00:19:08.230
The heat is moving?

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:09.890
Exactly.

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:15.480
From his palms to his chest,
stomach, and thighs.

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:17.730
It goes through the calf

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:20.280
and reaches his toes.

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:25.280
The chain of muscle movement
takes roughly 1.5 seconds.

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:28.080
The movement completes very quickly.

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:30.080
General.

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:36.130
Spec repeatedly does this all day
while he's awake.

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:40.550
Isn't Spec hospitalized right now?

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:42.590
Yes, he's bedridden.

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:43.970
The other day,

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:49.100
we sent this data to the Tokyo Sports
Physiology Research Center.

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:51.770
We received interesting news.

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:54.690
He's swimming.

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:57.110
He's swimming?

00:19:58.280 --> 00:19:59.610
Swimming?

00:20:00.190 --> 00:20:01.030
<i>Yes.</i>

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:04.530
<i>And it's the butterfly,</i>
<i>the most intense and exhausting form.</i>

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:08.120
He does the butterfly while in bed?

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:13.290
And what's more interesting
is that the color from the thermography

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:15.880
shows a higher output than swimming.

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:19.960
Spec isn't swimming in water.

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:23.430
Then what is he swimming in?

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:25.930
It's far more

00:20:27.510 --> 00:20:30.430
<i>high-viscosity and syrupy as a liquid.</i>

00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:36.650
He's forcing himself through a sea
of liquid that's far heavier than water.

00:20:38.570 --> 00:20:40.900
<i>It's a super-weighted butterfly.</i>

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:44.910
I wonder where his destination is.

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:05.090
What do you think, Sonoda?

00:21:05.720 --> 00:21:08.800
Even after looking at each inmate,
it doesn't make sense.

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:11.060
Their goals are unclear.

00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:13.310
But perhaps

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:17.230
it's the same as
when they gathered in Japan.

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:21.320
The same phenomenon may be happening
in separate places again.

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:24.820
-Synchronicity.
-Yes.

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:28.070
We can't rule out the possibility.

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:36.080
Looks like we'll need strict vigilance
and investigation, Inspector Sonoda.

00:21:36.540 --> 00:21:38.380
Yes, roger that!

00:23:42.290 --> 00:23:43.210
IDIOTS FROM PLANET STRONG

00:23:49.090 --> 00:23:51.010
Subtitle translation by Chul Kim
